## What NOT to Do

- ❌ Don't suggest adding features outside current phase
- ❌ Don't flag versions as invalid without verification
- ❌ Don't ignore existing patterns in the codebase
- ❌ Don't create files without being asked (especially .md files)
- ❌ Don't assume your training data is current for version info
- ❌ Don't suggest enterprise solutions for learning-scale problems
- ❌ Don't modify working code without a specific reason

## Remember

This is a **learning project**. The goal is understanding, not just completion.
Always explain the "why" behind suggestions and help build strong engineering habits.
